From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: ps5cemu <ps5cemu@localhost>
Date: Sat, 3 Oct 2026 16:00:08 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] aco: no external disassembler on the PS5

Without LLVM, check_print_asm_support asks system() whether the CLRX
disassembler is installed, for every shader compiled with its IR kept
(RADV_DEBUG=hang, shader dumps). The PS5 runs no other program, and the
call took about a second to fail: Breath of the Wild's pipeline cache
loaded at one pipeline a second with RADV_DEBUG=hang. On the PS5 there is
no disassembler to look for.
---
 src/amd/compiler/aco_print_asm.cpp | 8 +++++---
 1 file changed, 5 insertions(+), 3 deletions(-)

diff --git a/src/amd/compiler/aco_print_asm.cpp b/src/amd/compiler/aco_print_asm.cpp
index 01aee2a..7ab4554 100644
--- a/src/amd/compiler/aco_print_asm.cpp
+++ b/src/amd/compiler/aco_print_asm.cpp
@@ -421,12 +421,14 @@ check_print_asm_support(Program* program, enum radeon_family family)
    }
 #endif
 
-#ifndef _WIN32
+#if defined(_WIN32) || defined(__PROSPERO__)
+   /* The PS5 runs no other program: system() for the CLRX disassembler took about a second to
+    * fail, for every shader RADV_DEBUG=hang (or a shader dump) compiled. */
+   return false;
+#else
    /* Check if CLRX disassembler binary is available and can disassemble the program */
    return to_clrx_device_name(program->gfx_level, family) &&
           system("clrxdisasm --version > /dev/null 2>&1") == 0;
-#else
-   return false;
 #endif
 }
 
